                <pb facs="0511" n="431" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg431"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dudley to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-03-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 18,
                    1901</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Dudley reports that the Peruvian Government has offered 3,000 soles in
                    settlement of the claim of Fowks, with the proviso that such action is not
                    citable as a precedent; that he considers the offer equitable, and that the
                    claimant is anxious to accept it.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
